      "audioUrl": "/web-tieng-anh/audio/listening_8_ck2.mp3",
      "audioScript": "Ben: Hi Trang! What futuristic communication or scientific breakthrough are you presenting?\nTrang: Hi Ben! I am presenting about 3D Bioprinting Living Human Organs for Transplants at regenerative medicine lab.\nBen: What is the most astonishing feature of this innovation?\nTrang: Researchers and users are captivated by bio-ink stem cell printers and eager to test printing functional human organs.\nBen: How will it revolutionize human life or space exploration?\nTrang: It advances layer-by-layer tissue scaffolds and relies on the groundbreaking precision of nutrient perfusion incubator.\nBen: Incredible! That sounds like science fiction turning into scientific reality.",
      "clozeText": "Rapid advancements in science, communication, and astrophysics are redefining human capabilities. In regenerative medicine lab, scientists are developing bio-ink stem cell printers to unlock new frontiers in (23) ________. If these technologies mature, people will be able to practice printing functional human organs with unprecedented (24) ________. Many researchers reported that artificial intelligence (25) ________ transform daily healthcare and education. Furthermore, discovering layer-by-layer tissue scaffolds expands our understanding of life in the wider (26) ________. In conclusion, mastering nutrient perfusion incubator will ensure that humanity thrives in a technologically advanced (27) ________.",
      "readingText": "3D Bioprinting Living Human Organs for Transplants stands at the cutting edge of modern scientific inquiry and human imagination in regenerative medicine lab. By combining bio-ink stem cell printers with advanced computing power, this innovation significantly accelerates breakthroughs in layer-by-layer tissue scaffolds. Early clinical or laboratory trials involving printing functional human organs have demonstrated extraordinary increases in operational speed and user safety. Astrophysicists and biomedical engineers highlight nutrient perfusion incubator as the linchpin that makes these previously unimaginable feats possible. Moreover, whether enabling paralyzed patients to communicate or detecting habitable exoplanets, science enriches human dignity. As society navigates the ethical dimensions of advanced technologies, responsible innovation will guide human civilization toward cosmic wonders.",
      "passageText": "📖 ĐOẠN VĂN ĐIỀN TỪ (CLOZE TEXT):\nRapid advancements in science, communication, and astrophysics are redefining human capabilities. In regenerative medicine lab, scientists are developing bio-ink stem cell printers to unlock new frontiers in (23) ________. If these technologies mature, people will be able to practice printing functional human organs with unprecedented (24) ________. Many researchers reported that artificial intelligence (25) ________ transform daily healthcare and education. Furthermore, discovering layer-by-layer tissue scaffolds expands our understanding of life in the wider (26) ________. In conclusion, mastering nutrient perfusion incubator will ensure that humanity thrives in a technologically advanced (27) ________.\n\n📖 ĐOẠN VĂN ĐỌC HIỂU (READING PASSAGE):\n3D Bioprinting Living Human Organs for Transplants stands at the cutting edge of modern scientific inquiry and human imagination in regenerative medicine lab. By combining bio-ink stem cell printers with advanced computing power, this innovation significantly accelerates breakthroughs in layer-by-layer tissue scaffolds. Early clinical or laboratory trials involving printing functional human organs have demonstrated extraordinary increases in operational speed and user safety. Astrophysicists and biomedical engineers highlight nutrient perfusion incubator as the linchpin that makes these previously unimaginable feats possible. Moreover, whether enabling paralyzed patients to communicate or detecting habitable exoplanets, science enriches human dignity. As society navigates the ethical dimensions of advanced technologies, responsible innovation will guide human civilization toward cosmic wonders.",
      "writingRubric": "Bố cục rõ ràng (0.25đ) - Ngữ pháp & Từ vựng chính xác (0.5đ) - Tính liên kết mạch lạc (0.25đ)",
      "sampleWritingText": "In my view, 3D Bioprinting Living Human Organs for Transplants represents an astonishing leap for science and humanity. Located in regenerative medicine lab, it harnesses bio-ink stem cell printers to solve challenges that once seemed insurmountable. Enabling people to practice printing functional human organs expands our cognitive and technological horizons. Furthermore, the relentless precision of nutrient perfusion incubator paves the way for interstellar exploration. I am confident this innovation will shape a brighter tomorrow.",
